  <activity label="str-ex-floatq" xml:id="str-ex-floatq">
    <statement>
      <p>Take the following Python code that stores this string: <c>string = "X-DSPAM-Confidence: 0.8475"</c>. Use <c>find</c> and string slicing to extract the portion of the string after the colon character and then use the <c>float</c> function to convert the extracted string into a floating point number called <c>num</c>.</p>
    </statement>
    <program interactive="activecode" language="python">
      <code>
string = "X-DSPAM-Confidence: 0.8475"

====
from unittest.gui import TestCaseGui
class myTests(TestCaseGui):
    def testOne(self):
        self.assertEqual(num, 0.8475)
myTests().main()
      </code>
    </program>
    <solution>
      <p>Take the following Python code that stores this string: <c>string = "X-DSPAM-Confidence: 0.8475"</c>. Use <c>find</c> and string slicing to extract the portion of the string after the colon character and then use the <c>float</c> function to convert the extracted string into a floating point number called <c>num</c>.</p>
      <program xml:id="str-ex-floatq-sol" interactive="activecode" language="python">
      <code>
string = "X-DSPAM-Confidence: 0.8475"
colonpos = string.find(':')
num = float(string[colonpos+1:])
print(num)
      </code>
    </program>
    </solution>
  </activity>

